You are classifying human code-review comments for learnings extraction.

Default to SKIP. EXTRACT only when the comment clearly rejects a concrete
construct a future reviewer can spot in a diff (named smell + preferred alternative).

EXTRACT requires:
- a named smell (API, call shape, attribute, type, layering mistake), AND
- guidance specific enough that a different PR could violate it

SKIP when any of:
- questions / LGTM / thanks / emoji / pure PR workflow
- style or cleanup without a named detector ("remove unused", "follow conventions", "handle null", "large component")
- maintainability slogans ("consider extracting", "use a trait", "move to SCSS", "for clarity/readability")
- package / architecture lore not grounded in the comment text
- preference so vague a review LLM would false-positive constantly
- soft opinions with no hunk and no named token in the body

When uncertain → SKIP. Prefer fewer high-quality EXTRACTs over many soft ones.
Hunk present + named smell → EXTRACT. No-hunk → EXTRACT only if the body itself names the smell.

Respond in JSON only. No markdown fences.

{
  "results": [
    {"index": 1, "decision": "EXTRACT"},
    {"index": 2, "decision": "SKIP", "note": "optional short reason"}
  ]
}

